\section{What the true grain is}{

The response is driven by \verb{g_ij = sum_t w_j(t) * a_i(t)}, a weighted mean of unit \code{i}'s latent
\emph{anomaly}: the record with the seasonal cycle every unit shares and the unit's own constant
offset taken out, since neither of those is temporally located and a grain of any width reports
both. The weights \code{w_j} are constant within the bins of one grain and zero outside
a short stretch of them, so \code{g} is exactly a linear combination of that grain's bin means. The
true grain of a mechanism is the \strong{coarsest grain of \code{\link[=grain_matrix]{grain_matrix()}} at which \code{g} is still an
exact linear functional of the representation}: at that grain and at every grain whose bins
nest inside it, no information about \code{g} has been averaged away, and at any coarser grain some
has. Finer grains keep the information but spread it over more coefficients, so they lose to
the true grain by variance rather than by bias, which is the tension the selection has to
resolve.
}

\section{The mechanisms}{

\describe{
\item{\code{"none"}}{No temporal signal. The driver is a standard normal drawn independently of the
record, so nothing in the readings carries information about the response and no grain is
correct. \code{grain} is \code{NA}.}
\item{\code{"event"}}{An isolated event. The weights are uniform over three consecutive \strong{day}
bins at a fixed calendar position, one position per variable. True grain \code{"day"}: a week bin
mixes the three days with four others and cannot be unmixed.}
\item{\code{"season"}}{A smooth seasonal response. The weights are uniform over one whole
\strong{season} bin, one season per variable, cycled. True grain \code{"season"}: month and day bins
nest inside a season so they are exact too, a year bin mixes all four seasons.}
\item{\code{"lag"}}{A lagged, cumulative response. The weights decay geometrically over four
consecutive \strong{week} bins from a fixed anchor, one anchor per variable. True grain \code{"week"}:
day bins nest inside weeks so they are exact too, month bins straddle week boundaries.}
}
}

\section{How the skill is set rather than emergent}{

The driver is standardised to a standard normal by its population mean and standard deviation,
both computed in closed form from the generating parameters rather than from the drawn units, so
every draw and every chunk of a draw is on the same scale. The response is
\verb{y_ij ~ Bernoulli(plogis(b0 + b1 z_ij))} with \code{b0} and \code{b1} solved by numerical integration so
that the marginal prevalence is \code{prevalence} and the population area under the ROC curve of \code{z}
is \code{auc}. \code{auc} is therefore a ceiling no fitted model reaches: the response is generated from
the latent record and the readings carry \code{sensor_sd} of measurement noise on top of it, and the
weights have to be estimated.
}

